.th TTYN III 5/31/77
.sh NAME
ttyn \*- return name of current terminal
.sh SYNOPSIS
.ft B
jsr	pc,ttyn
.s3
ttyn(file)
.s3
.ft R
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it Ttyn
hunts up the last character of the name of the
terminal which is the standard input (from \fIas\fR)
or is specified by the
argument
.it file
descriptor (from C).
If \fIn\fR is returned, the
terminal name is then ``/dev/tty\fIn\fR''.
.s3
.bd x
is returned if the indicated file does not correspond to a
terminal.
